From 7e1f5eb6703d4db15d2e53329bb034257130f66f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:51:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ExactMeshArrangement: Orient and InCircle beyond the fixed
 width on stack limbs

The last stage of ExactMeshArrangement.Orient and InCircle for points beyond the fixed width was a BigInteger 3 x 3
determinant (12.4 million calls in the difference of 55928 with its rotated copy, nearly half of its allocation).
ExactLimbSigns.Orient2 and InCircle evaluate the same determinants on stack limbs with FixedArith; beyond the stack
limit of Det4 (operands and scratch space above 4608 limbs) and on netstandard2.0 they evaluate the BigInteger form
themselves (Orient2Big, InCircleBig). The arrangement's two BigInteger determinants and incircle_row move there; the
call sites multiply the kernel's sign by the projection's.

Scratch space: OrientScratch = 6 a + 15 (b + c) + 32 (need at most 5 a + 14 (b + c) + 11), InCircleScratch =
28 p + 46 (q + r) + 128 (need at most 27 p + 45 (q + r) + 99); derivation in docs/design/EXACT_LIMB_SIGNS.md, section 5.

Measured against the kernels of #772 (4 cores, wall time with collections, median of 5): 55928 352.8 -> 310.4 s
(-12.0 %), allocation 180 -> 94 GB; 107554, 42327 and the normal stratum unchanged within the run-to-run range;
hashes equal.

Tests: ExactLimbSignsTestsPlanar (reference determinants written in the test, known signs, paths, scratch use, the
limits in the three projections), ExactBooleanWidePointTests (through ExactMeshBoolean with BigInteger points and
the filters off: results, invariance, reuse, serial against parallel, the allocation bound). The offsets of the
shards mesh-arrangement-2..4 follow the file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AaGT5CdtKaF4p9ewMMrjAm
